---
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import "./dunstkreis.css";
import Try from "../Try.astro";
import Shown from "./Shown.astro";
import "./starve.css";

/** Every table with the range of sizes and sample counts it can be set to; the defaults are dunstkreis' own. */
const TABLES = [
    {
        name: "transmittance",
        title: "Transmittance",
        axes: "view angle × altitude",
        width: { min: 8, max: 1024, presets: [64, 128, 256, 512, 1024] },
        height: { min: 4, max: 256, presets: [16, 32, 64, 128, 256] },
        samples: {
            min: 1,
            max: 512,
            step: 1,
            label: "samples per ray to the top",
            title: "Integration samples along the ray from the texel's point to the top of the atmosphere. With refraction, 18 bent rays per texel find the one arriving from its direction.",
        },
        x: ["straight up", "view angle, spaced by the distance to the top", "just below the horizon"],
        y: ["top", "altitude", "ground"],
    },
    {
        name: "multiScattering",
        title: "Multiple scattering",
        axes: "sun angle × altitude",
        width: { min: 4, max: 512, presets: [32, 64, 128, 256, 512] },
        height: { min: 4, max: 256, presets: [16, 32, 64, 128, 256] },
        samples: {
            min: 1,
            max: 64,
            step: 1,
            label: "samples per ray, 64 rays",
            title: "Integration samples along each of the 8 × 8 rays a texel sends out over the sphere to gather light scattered once more.",
        },
        x: ["sun −90°", "sun elevation", "sun +90°"],
        y: ["top", "altitude", "ground"],
    },
    {
        name: "skyView",
        title: "Sky view",
        axes: "azimuth from the Sun × angle from the horizon",
        width: { min: 8, max: 1024, presets: [32, 64, 128, 256, 512] },
        height: { min: 4, max: 1024, presets: [64, 128, 256, 512, 1024] },
        samples: {
            min: 1,
            max: 128,
            step: 1,
            label: "samples per view ray",
            title: "Integration samples along each texel's view ray, out to the ground or the top of the atmosphere. From above the atmosphere the sky pass raymarches every pixel with as many.",
        },
        x: ["away from the Sun", "the Sun, mirrored at it", "away from it"],
        y: ["zenith", "angle from the horizon, which is in the middle", "nadir"],
    },
];
// The sky view's axes, which the other tables' heat maps take on when they show their effect on the sky.
const SKY = TABLES[2] ?? TABLES[0];
const TICKS = [0.1, 1, 10, 100];
---

<figure class="scene-frame" id="tables">
    <div class="lut-bar">
        <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-field="reset" title="Back to dunstkreis' defaults">defaults</button>
        <span class="note" data-field="timing"></span>
        <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-field="starve-toggle" aria-pressed="false" title="Each table against a reference with many more texels and samples, as a heat map of the difference">vs. reference</button>
        {
            import.meta.env.DEV && (
                <span class="starve-variants">
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-variant="A" title="Each table against its reference, in its own texels">variant A</button>
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-variant="B" title="What each table's difference makes of the sky view, everything else at the reference">variant B</button>
                </span>
            )
        }
    </div>
    <div class="starve-legend" data-field="starve-legend" hidden>
        <span class="starve-scale">
            <span class="starve-ramp" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="starve-ticks">{TICKS.map((t) => <span>{t}%</span>)}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="note" data-field="starve-total"></span>
        <span class="note" data-field="starve-status"></span>
    </div>
    {
        TABLES.map((table) => (
            <section class="lut" data-lut={table.name}>
                <p class="lut-head">
                    <strong>{table.title}</strong> <span class="note">{table.axes}</span>
                </p>
                <div class="lut-call" data-field="call" />
                <div class="lut-plot">
                    <span class="lut-axis lut-y">
                        {table.y.map((label, i) => (
                            <span data-sky={table === SKY ? undefined : SKY.y[i]}>{label}</span>
                        ))}
                    </span>
                    <div class="lut-stage">
                        <canvas data-field="image" aria-label={`The ${table.title.toLowerCase()} table`} />
                        <canvas data-field="heat" class="starve-heat" aria-hidden="true" hidden />
                        <canvas data-field="overlay" aria-hidden="true" />
                        <span class="lut-size" data-field="size" />
                        <div class="lut-tip" data-field="tip" hidden />
                    </div>
                    <span class="lut-axis lut-x">
                        {table.x.map((label, i) => (
                            <span data-sky={table === SKY ? undefined : SKY.x[i]}>{label}</span>
                        ))}
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p class="note starve-stats" data-field="starve" hidden />
                <details class="fold lut-fold">
                    <summary>
                        <span class="moment-title">Settings</span> <span class="note" data-field="summary" />
                    </summary>
                    <p class="lut-controls">
                        <span class="lut-role">computed</span>
                        <input
                            type="number"
                            data-config={`${table.name}.width`}
                            min={table.width.min}
                            max={table.width.max}
                            step="1"
                            aria-label={`${table.title} width`}
                        />
                        ×
                        <input
                            type="number"
                            data-config={`${table.name}.height`}
                            min={table.height.min}
                            max={table.height.max}
                            step="1"
                            aria-label={`${table.title} height`}
                        />
                        {(["width", "height"] as const).map((axis) => (
                            <span class="steps" role="radiogroup" aria-label={`${table.title} ${axis}`}>
                                {table[axis].presets.map((n) => (
                                    <label>
                                        <input
                                            type="radio"
                                            name={`${table.name}-${axis}`}
                                            value={n}
                                            data-preset={`${table.name}.${axis}`}
                                        />
                                        <span>{n}</span>
                                    </label>
                                ))}
                            </span>
                        ))}
                    </p>
                    <p class="lut-controls lut-indent">
                        <label title={table.samples.title}>
                            {table.samples.label}
                            <input
                                type="range"
                                data-config={`integralSamples.${table.name}`}
                                min={table.samples.min}
                                max={table.samples.max}
                                step={table.samples.step}
                            />
                            <output />
                        </label>
                        <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-refraction aria-pressed="true" title="Traced through the air, bending the light. Switches it for the whole page, recomputing every table and cube map">refracted</button>
                        <span class="note" data-field="info" />
                    </p>
                    <Shown name={table.name} title={table.title} />
                </details>
            </section>
        ))
    }
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The tables behind the sky above, as they are right now, and what they are computed with. Transmittance and
        multiple scattering change only with the air; the sky view with every move of the Sun or the observer. Shown
        tone mapped, each by its own scale; point at a texel to read what it stands for. Against the reference, each a
        heat map of how far it lies from one with many more texels and samples, on a log scale from dark, 0.1% or less,
        to light, 100%, black where too dark to measure; under it that difference, and the one it makes in the sky view
        with every other table at the reference.
        <Try label="Potsdam in twilight" set="date=2026-04-06T19:10Z&lat=52.395&lon=13.085&h=1" fig="tables">
            against the reference, the multiple scattering moves the sky by almost 1% on average, more than the other two
            tables together.
        </Try>
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./tables";
</script>
